<title>USA: Alpha to take Q4 charge for unit sales.</title>
<headline>Alpha to take Q4 charge for unit sales.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Industries Inc said it will take  a one-time charge of not more than $4.9 million in the fourth quarter ending March 31, 1997 for the divestiture of units.</p>
<p>Alpha said it has sold its Trans-Tech Europe manufacturing subsidiary in France to NewCo Ceramiques, a French manufacturer of industrial and medical ceramics, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Alpha also said it has sold its Digital Radio Components product line to Advanced Frequency Products, a newly formed company for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The company said that as previously projected, these actions have reduced Alpha's quarterly break-even point to $21-22 million.</p>
